// Device spec §1 "Split registries" and spec §20.3.1: cast_device_registered sends to the device
// worker (spawn_device_registered) that holds the name in the device registry when the message is
// sent, and raises actor_not_found when no worker holds it, as cast_registered does. Here the caller
// is main, so the failure is the language-level failure of §15.4.5.5: the failure atom's name on
// the console and exit status 1; nothing after the cast runs. The runtimes once answered an unheld
// device name with a silent false. Board-only, like the other device trials; the module name begins
// with device_ because only a device_ module may name the device surface (E2232).
//
// Expected output:
//   before
//   actor_not_found
// exit status 1

fn main() -> int64 {
    sequence proc[concurrency, device_io]
        println("before");
        _: boolean <- cast_device_registered(:device_nobody_holds_this, { op: :init, byte: 0 } impl ActorMessage {});
        println("not reached")
    produces
        pure 0
    end
}
